# OS / editor junk
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# The raw dataset and its build scripts live on the dev-data branch, not here.
# Ignored rather than merely absent so a maintainer can drop the folder back in
# place — git archive dev-data | tar -x — without cluttering git status.
# The dataset and sprites are ~250 MB and already tracked on `main` at the repo
# root, so this branch does not carry a second copy. Restore it into a fresh
# checkout with:
#     git archive origin/main app-data | tar -x -C "PDS React Develop"
PDS React Develop/app-data/

# Release staging, built by tools/make-release.sh on the dev-data branch. It has
# to sit inside the project: gh runs on the host and cannot see the sandbox /tmp.
dist/

# Personal campaign data — keep the sample structure, not real sheets
# The rulebook PDFs are the reader's own copy and are not ours to redistribute.
# Nothing else stopped `git add -A` from staging one.
PDS React Develop/Pokerole Core Book/*.pdf
!PDS React Develop/Pokerole Core Book/Instructions.txt

PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/*.json
PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Custom Images/Trainers/*
PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Custom Images/Pokemons/*
PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Wild Pokemons/*

# ...but keep the folder placeholders and the intentional sample image
!PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Custom Images/Trainers/.gitkeep
!PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Wild Pokemons/.gitkeep
!PDS React Develop/Trainers and Pokemons/Custom Images/Pokemons/My Misdreavus <3 (is a she).png

# Local development notes — machine-specific, not part of the project
CLAUDE.md

# Working notes on the equipment icon picks — kept locally, not shipped
EQUIPMENT-ICONS.md

# Demo recordings for the README, and the GIFs built from them. Hosted outside
# the app download: both release zips are built from git refs, so anything
# committed here would land in every download of the app.
gifs/

# The publishable copy of the app. Generated by `npm run deploy` from
# "PDS React Develop/", and rebuilt from scratch by the Pages workflow — never
# edited by hand.
#
# Generated rather than committed for three reasons, none of them pack size:
# git is content-addressed, so a second copy of identical files costs tree
# entries, not blobs.
#   1. tools/make-release.sh archives `main` wholesale, so a tracked duplicate
#      would double the download people actually want.
#   2. Every clone and CI checkout would carry another 250 MB of working tree.
#   3. The dedup only holds while the copies are byte-identical. One re-encoded
#      PNG or rewritten bundle and that file's full size is in the pack forever.
PDS React Deploy/

# Node toolchain, and the folder the app build is assembled in. `dist/` above is
# the release-zip staging from tools/make-release.sh; these never tread on each
# other. The finished pages and assets/ are copied from dist-pwa/ into
# "PDS React Develop/" and ARE committed — they are what a download opens.
node_modules/
dist-pwa/

# Screenshots and scratch files from scripts/compare-ui.sh
.verify/
